<p>Due to a Commission holiday, no ECU rates were published today. Therefore, Friday's scenario remains unchanged, with the UK average RMG above +5 per cent at 5.350 per cent. It is therefore currently forecast to enter a fifth and final confirmation period on 26 May, prior to a possible revaluation on 5 June. All currencies with negative RMGs for this period will be devalued on 26 May by reducing their negative gaps to zero. Hence a devaluation is currently forecast for the Belgian and Greek green rates.</p>
